>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/tree/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQM/tree/ece824419c9006fe66436daf233822b75533b82f/tmQM"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Site-by-site g-xTB correction of ligand connectivity. The three P–alkyl-C distances at six-coordinate P6 are 2.005, 2.015 and 2.006 Å. The respective g-xTB bond orders are 0.781, 0.762 and 0.778. Restoring P6–C63 makes C63 neutral and tetravalent, P6 has six single bonds and carries −1. Retain the other local charges. The donor–acceptor or covalent assignment of P9–N41 requires separate review. Localized 10 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

