>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Mo–N–O 170.29°, N–O 1.19777 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.5216. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +2 and total charge +0. Neutral Cp*Mo(NO)(η²-benzyl)Cl in Figure 1 and Table IV. Cp*, benzyl and Cl each carry −1. The Mo(II)/NO⁺ limiting form conserves charge; The original same-ID table gives N#O. Localized 11 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 43 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 40 nonmetal covalent bonds: 39 within range, 0 outside range and 1 with sparse controls.

